WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.930
A selfless public
servant, Vice Admiral T-Bone,

3
00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:36.240
<b>Marine Headquarters</b>

4
00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:34.720
was beloved by Marines
and citizens alike.

5
00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:38.950
<b>Vice Admiral T-Bone Dead</b>

6
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.560
His sudden death
shocked the world.

7
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.490
<b>Marine Headquarters</b>

8
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.350
The Navy announced that
he died in the line of duty,

9
00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:43.210
<b>Marine Headquarters 
Vice Admiral T-Bone Dead</b>

10
00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.930
but provided no details.

11
00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:46.080
Have they
found the killer yet?

12
00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:48.050
<b>Let's Go and Take It!</b>

13
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.730
I'm not sure.

14
00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.130
But we've been keeping
an eye on the family,

15
00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.080
and they seem to be
living comfortably.

16
00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:56.080
Of course they are.
What a mess.

17
00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.500
Never imagined
I'd live in a world

18
00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:00.070
where Marines are
murdered by civilians.

19
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.950
Pirates aren't the only
ones who want money.

20
00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.600
This was inevitable from
the moment we received bounties.

21
00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.760
T-Bone was killed
in Pepe Kingdom,

22
00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.010
where over a thousand
people starve every year.

23
00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:14.810
It's certainly no excuse,
but poverty can drive

24
00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:17.220
even the sanest
men to madness.

25
00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.890
If this was all
the Genius Jester's plan,

26
00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.270
then we've
underestimated him.

27
00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:24.750
How can we expect
our men to risk their lives

28
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.780
to save citizens who
are out for their blood?

29
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.720
We need to destroy
Cross Guild soon.

30
00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.170
Morale is more essential
than you'd think.

31
00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.780
A seed of doubt can become
a deadly poison.

32
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:36.390
<b>Marine Headquarters 
Vice Admiral T-Bone Dead</b>

33
00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.420
Oh, Hina!

34
00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:42.230
Hmm?

35
00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.020
Have you seen Garp today?

36
00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.390
I've got some new
crackers I want him to try!

37
00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.990
Yeah, about that...

38
00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.660
He set off a while ago.

39
00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.240
Huh? Rescue Koby?

40
00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:55.000
I think he may have taken
some members of SWORD with him.

41
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.920
Which means Kujaku
is probably there.

42
00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.180
What?!

43
00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.980
You're saying they
went to Fullalead?

44
00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.960
<b>Empty Bluffs Island
New World</b>

45
00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:09.890
So you survived your long
journey across the sea.

46
00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:10.820
Yes, sir.

47
00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.270
Excellent work!

48
00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:16.250
The whole criminal world
is singing your praises!

49
00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.430
Three cheers for you,
our evil star!

50
00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:23.090
Yeah!

51
00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.660
I heard the news, sir,

52
00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.710
that you sent
the money to my family.

53
00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.880
Thank you, I owe you my life!

54
00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.290
Think nothing of it!

55
00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:34.150
You singlehandedly killed
a vice admiral in cold blood!

56
00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.760
Such villainy
deserves a reward!

57
00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.250
From what I hear,
those poor Marines

58
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.250
still haven't gotten over it!

59
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.020
You'd better hope that
they don't find you!

60
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.950
They'll chop
your pretty head off!

61
00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.830
I know I can never go back
home to my family again,

62
00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:57.070
but it's better than letting
them starve to death!

63
00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.660
Don't worry, pal!

64
00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:02.450
Once you join my crew,
you'll have a whole new family!

65
00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:03.650
Join your crew?

66
00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.710
Welcome to the team, pal!

67
00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.400
No, I... I could never.

68
00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.180
You don't get it, do ya?

69
00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:10.030
Huh?

70
00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:13.640
Our chairman ain't just
a pirate, he's an Emperor!

71
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.780
Most pirates don't even
get to look at the man,

72
00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.940
let alone sail by his side!

73
00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.950
And yet there he is!
The real deal!

74
00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.760
The bona fide Buggy!

75
00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:26.250
Yeah! Bona fide!

76
00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:27.910
Bona fide Buggy...!

77
00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.730
I like that, it's catchy!

78
00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.090
Excuse me, Chairman
Boney-Thighed Buggy?

79
00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.980
My thighs are super shapely!

80
00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:49.260
I have good news, sir!
Cross Guild's ship is all done!

81
00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.270
Don't worry about the ship!

82
00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.730
I got a team of pros that'll
whip up a real masterpiece!

83
00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:56.590
Like me!

84
00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.390
That's right!

85
00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:00.820
We're crazy about you!

86
00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.020
This is the king of ships!

87
00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:02.770
Do you love it or what?

88
00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.000
We're so good at this!

89
00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.150
This is how I die!

90
00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.530
Hey, that had better
not be our ship.

91
00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.810
Surely you
don't expect me to sail

92
00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.400
on that ridiculous-
looking thing.

93
00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:18.580
Meeting room. Now.

94
00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:23.750
It's not my fault!

95
00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.770
<b>Meeting Room</b>

96
00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.980
Cross Guild's public
reception has been excellent.

97
00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.200
Now that our name's
out there,

98
00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.150
the Navy will wake up
to the threat that we pose.

99
00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:44.500
Please kill me.
I'm begging you. It hurts.

100
00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.480
Our goal is to create a utopia.

101
00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.580
A military nation
that won't bow

102
00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.570
to the Governmentor,
or to anyone else.

103
00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.000
And for that, only one
thing is necessary.

104
00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.040
An overwhelming
amount of strength.

105
00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.330
This is not the life
I envisioned for myself.

106
00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.010
I'm in hell!

107
00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.990
But in order to acquire
the strength we need, first we...

108
00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:05.080
We need "wealth,
fame, and power"?

109
00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:06.050
Huh?

110
00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.800
Sorry. I got a bit
carried away.

111
00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.080
Shut your mouth.

112
00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:13.490
Screw this!

113
00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.460
If you wanna shut me up
that bad, just kill me already!

114
00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:19.130
But I'll tell you one last thing!

115
00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.050
These goals you're
chasing are small-time!

116
00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:24.450
How can your call yourself
a pirate, thinking like that?

117
00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.410
What's this? Desperation?

118
00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:27.680
You heard, right?

119
00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:31.430
Red Hair finally decided it
was time to make his move.

120
00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:34.170
He and I both rode on Roger's
ship back in his prime,

121
00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:35.470
but for one reason or another,

122
00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:39.270
we didn't make it
to Laugh Tale in the end.

123
00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.880
When you took to the sea,
you had a dream, too, right?

124
00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:45.570
Honestly, when I saw
how much potential

125
00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.500
Shanks had back then,

126
00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.710
I gave up my dream...
I let it die!

127
00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.810
<b>24 Years Ago

The Day of
Gold Roger's Execution</b>

128
00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:56.740
I haven't forgotten
what you said, Shanks!

129
00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.800
You said you'd make it to Laugh
Tale on your ship. You swore!

130
00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:03.430
Yeah. But I changed my mind.

131
00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.580
That's not what I wanna
fight for right now.

132
00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:06.790
Huh?!

133
00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.940
I'll still
be a pirate, though.

134
00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.880
I thought you were
better than that, Shanks.

135
00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.830
I thought you'd be
the one leading the charge

136
00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.770
for the next
generation of pirates!

137
00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:19.830
Come with me,
Buggy. You'll see.

138
00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:21.230
You think I wanna
work for you

139
00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.940
after that crap
you just told me?

140
00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.690
You're a damn coward!

141
00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.860
Captain Roger wanted
you to follow in his footsteps!

142
00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:29.430
Can't you see that?

143
00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:31.980
I lost my treasure
map because of you!

144
00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.350
I'm sure you wanna
blow that off,

145
00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:36.300
like you do everything
else, but I'm still angry!

146
00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:40.550
In fact, from now
on, you're my enemy!

147
00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.730
Now he suddenly
changes his mind?

148
00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.320
After all this time?

149
00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.790
To hell with him!

150
00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:51.920
Even if I just got lucky,
I am an Emperor, same as him!

151
00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:56.250
I want to be king!

152
00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:59.690
The King of the Pirates!

153
00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:03.910
Wealth! Fame!
And power, too!

154
00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:06.640
We just have to find it!

155
00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:09.750
Roger's treasure
is waiting for us!

156
00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:12.780
Stop!

157
00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.330
That's enough out of you!

158
00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:33.150
Seems your new title has given
you delusions of grandeur.

159
00:08:33.230 --> 00:08:35.420
Should we beat some
more sense into you?

160
00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:38.970
Did you honestly think your insipid
speech would work on us?

161
00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:41.610
Piracy is a business,
not some little game.

162
00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:43.740
You think you can be
king without a plan? Fool.

163
00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.740
Red Hair, Blackbeard,
and Straw Hat.

164
00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.020
Those are the enemies
we would have to face.

165
00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:51.920
Yeah, but we
can outsmart them!

166
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.320
A treasure hunt is
a race, not a war!

167
00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:57.680
You made fun of my speech?

168
00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:01.740
I'll show you how
inspirational I can be!

169
00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:03.990
Why do you think
pirates took to the sea?

170
00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:07.400
To chase dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

171
00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:08.750
Hm?

172
00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:10.800
Listen up, men!

173
00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.400
Chairman Buggy?

174
00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.920
Don't
you even think about it!

175
00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:24.810
Ahem. C'mon, tell me!

176
00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:27.840
What dream drove
you to the sea?

177
00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:31.270
In our world, you could die
before you know it!

178
00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.660
Aren't your souls crying
out for something

179
00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:36.910
that's worth fighting for?

180
00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:47.380
Ah! He's right! I can feel it!

181
00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.760
My lost passion is
coming back to life!

182
00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:53.730
Only a coward would be
satisfied with the status quo!

183
00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:54.760
If you have a dream,

184
00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.890
then chase it with all
your strength!

185
00:09:56.890 --> 00:10:00.560
I've got your backs;
there's no need to fear!

186
00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:07.010
There's only one goal for us
now... the One Piece!

187
00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:10.960
What?

188
00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:21.940
I can see the ship!

189
00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.770
<b>Deputy Commander Ushiano
(Morley's Subordinate)
Western Division
Revolutionary Army</b>

190
00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:25.510
You okay, pal? Just breathe,
we're almost there.

191
00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:26.790
Keep it together!

192
00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:29.110
<b>Kamabakka Queendom
Grand Line</b>

193
00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:32.570
<b>Deputy Commander Ahiru
(Belo Betty's Subordinate)
Eastern Division
Revolutionary Army</b>

194
00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:39.740
<b>Deputy Commander Jiron
(Karasu's Subordinate)
Northern Division
Revolutionary Army</b>

195
00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.650
Hey, Ahiru!

196
00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:46.040
Hey, Ahiru! What'cha think?
A good ship? Or bad ship?

197
00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.720
Is it a friend? Enemy?
Who? What? How?

198
00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:51.380
Y'know, I bet they can see us.

199
00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:56.100
Quiet, I need to focus.
Kshoooo.

200
00:10:57.590 --> 00:11:01.180
Whirrr. Clang! Clunk!

201
00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:06.050
Gah!

202
00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.360
Say, would you
care to make a bet?

203
00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:10.320
Hm?

204
00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:15.240
<b>Deputy Commander Gambo
(Lindbergh's Subordinate)
Southern Division
Revolutionary Army</b>

205
00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.610
On what sort of ship
that is I mean.

206
00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:15.990
I wager it's an enemy!
Are you in?

207
00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:19.660
Jeah. Okay.

208
00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:22.360
Whoosh.

209
00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:30.180
Jou're on, my friend.

210
00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:33.100
I'll bet that's Sabo's ship.
How's a million sound?

211
00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:37.100
What?! A million?

212
00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:52.910
Dragon! Iva!

213
00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:58.040
It's Sabo! He finally
came home to us!

214
00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:03.000
Heehaw!
That's our boy!

215
00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.760
Why, I wasn't worried one bit!

216
00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:06.180
I've missed him so much!

217
00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:08.850
Sabo!

218
00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:26.660
Sabo!

219
00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:49.160
Hey, guys! It's been a while!

220
00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:52.910
Welcome back, Sabo!

221
00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:57.860
Damn you, Jirohn!
I know you cheated somehow!

222
00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.640
I won't give you one berry!

223
00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:02.390
Sorry, pal. But I won
the bet fair and square.

224
00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:06.500
Huh? What is that? Are
you eating a telescope?

225
00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:07.660
I dunno.

226
00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:11.010
Lying fraud!
Open your mouth!

227
00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:15.320
Whirrr. Clang!

228
00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:18.370
Welcome back! I was
just about to shoot you.

229
00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.600
Well, I'm glad
you didn't, Ahiru.

230
00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.040
Were you worried about me?

231
00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.790
– Maybe!
– Sabo!

232
00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.130
I'm so
happy you're safe!

233
00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:28.850
Hey, thanks, Ushiano.
Nice to see you.

234
00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.020
Y'little scamp!

235
00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:32.310
Don't you know it's rude
to keep a queen waiting?

236
00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:35.130
We were all in a stew
waiting for news!

237
00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.810
It's been quite the journey.

238
00:13:36.890 --> 00:13:39.370
Well, stop teasing
and spill the tea!

239
00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:42.590
For starters,
this ship is from Lulusia.

240
00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:44.630
The kingdom that just
vanished into thin air?

241
00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.890
Lulusia?

242
00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:47.320
Yeah. I'll explain things later.

243
00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:51.790
For now, we should find
them a place to rest.

244
00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:53.720
Hey! Sabo!

245
00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:00.510
How dare you go
radio silent on us!

246
00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.830
I'm sorry, but I
didn't have a choice!

247
00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.560
I couldn't get an encrypted
Transponder Snail.

248
00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:08.110
They were gonna tap the line!

249
00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:09.930
I couldn't risk
talking any longer!

250
00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:10.930
But you guys did hear me

251
00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:12.780
give the indirect
call signal, right?

252
00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:14.100
The three knocks.

253
00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:16.500
I was out of Lulusia,
perfectly safe.

254
00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:17.960
Alright!

255
00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:19.510
Yeah.

256
00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:24.350
But don't ever make me
worry like that again okay?

257
00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:26.830
Okay, sorry!

258
00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:27.710
Ah!

259
00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:39.370
Sabo! You
scared us half to death!

260
00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:42.660
Why do you men
always have to leave?

261
00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:44.420
Uh. Hi, Morley.

262
00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:52.140
If you ever break my heart
like that again, I'll... I'll...

263
00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:57.650
Aw! I can't stay mad at you,
I'm so glad you're back!

264
00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.430
Nice
to see you again.

265
00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:00.720
Hello!

266
00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:04.690
I remember you. You're
the chumps from Lulusia.

267
00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.780
I'm sorry you lost your home.

268
00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:10.200
I heard you wanna join
the Revolutionary Army?

269
00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:12.550
Yes, ma'am! We're ready!

270
00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:14.070
Not yet,
you're not!

271
00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.850
Get some rest first.
Sort out your feelings.

272
00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.940
I heard what
happened with Kuma.

273
00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:29.920
I'm sorry. It seems
we've wasted your time.

274
00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:31.100
If they programmed Kuma

275
00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:33.670
to return
to Mary Geoise automatically,

276
00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:36.340
our efforts may have
been futile from the start.

277
00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:37.420
Maybe so.

278
00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:41.510
I know this is hard on you two,
more than anyone else.

279
00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:43.440
Listen, getting
back to business,

280
00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.020
you can't even share
your news with the captains?

281
00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.870
No.
It's too dangerous.

282
00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:51.440
This is something I
can only share with you.

283
00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:52.720
What is it?

284
00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.530
The truth about what
happened at Mary Geoise.

285
00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:59.840
I'm going to tell you everything
about what I saw that day,

286
00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:01.370
the day of the Reverie.

287
00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.840
We managed to accomplish
all of our missions.

288
00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:08.380
There were three
general objectives.

289
00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.730
We declared war
on the Celestial Dragons

290
00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:12.810
by destroying their symbol.

291
00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:15.480
Then we set as many
of their slaves free as we could,

292
00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:17.690
including Kuma, of course,

293
00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:21.990
and then we destroyed
the food reserves in Mary Geoise.

294
00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.480
What results have you seen?

295
00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:26.740
Well, we've
caught the world's attention,

296
00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:28.540
which was the point.

297
00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.910
The Navy forces were
busy chasing you,

298
00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:32.980
so things worked
out conveniently.

299
00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:36.920
In short, 12 different countries
revolted against the Government.

300
00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.160
With our encouragement,
that is.

301
00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:41.170
It wasn't flawless of course,

302
00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:44.450
but eight of the revolts
were successful.

303
00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:47.620
The newspapers called it
the "Eight-Nation Revolution."

304
00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:51.460
Though I suppose seven
would be more accurate,

305
00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:56.170
now that Lulusia has vanished.

306
00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:58.290
One detail wasn't reported.

307
00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:01.520
Our forces have been
starving out the enemy.

308
00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:04.680
Seven nations have declined
to pay their Heavenly Tributes

309
00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:07.900
and have stopped exporting
resources to the Government.

310
00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:09.690
Yes,
not to mention,

311
00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:13.150
we've been attacking Government
shipments all over the world,

312
00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:16.450
completely cutting off
Mary Geoise's supplies.

313
00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:20.230
<b>The Holy Land
Mary Geoise</b>

314
00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:19.120
We were warned the capital
would be impenetrable

315
00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:21.620
because it's so high
above sea level.

316
00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:25.680
But who cares about position
when we've got attrition?

317
00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:27.180
Let them hide!

318
00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.900
They won't last a week
without money or food!

319
00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:33.570
Heehaw!

320
00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:35.580
Think we'll see
a response soon?

321
00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:38.100
Given our enemy, yes.

322
00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.360
The nobles are used
to getting what they want,

323
00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:42.020
when they want it.

324
00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:44.110
For those who have
known nothing but luxury,

325
00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:47.610
this will be pure torment.

326
00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:49.770
They're not the sort
of people who will sit back

327
00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:52.570
and endure an insult like this.

328
00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:55.300
They're going to dispatch
the Holy Knights.

329
00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:57.580
That's when the real
battle begins.

330
00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:58.690
Sabo!

331
00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:01.490
No, Flame Emperor Boy!

332
00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:04.910
You are at the top
of the Government's hit list now!

333
00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:07.940
Can we please drop
the nickname? It's ridiculous.

334
00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:11.250
Like it or not, it's the name
that made you an icon.

335
00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:13.570
I know you didn't kill him,

336
00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:16.130
but being framed
for Cobra's murder

337
00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:18.660
has made you a hero
to rebels worldwide.

338
00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.890
And many of those rebels
hold a common view:

339
00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.620
that anyone who is involved

340
00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:28.840
with the World
Government must be evil.

341
00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:31.630
Of course, the truth
isn't black and white.

342
00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.500
Even if the system is rotten,

343
00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:37.880
there are good kings
alongside all the tyrants.

344
00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:41.320
King Cobra of Alabasta
was well liked

345
00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:45.970
and had a reputation as
a kind and wise ruler.

346
00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:49.760
But reputations can be
deceiving sometimes.

347
00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:51.540
I agree.

348
00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:55.510
Cobra was a victim,
and his death was a tragedy.

349
00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:59.830
But if it fueled the rebellion,
then it was necessary!

350
00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:02.830
You've got conviction.

351
00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:07.260
In that case,
tell us everything.

